      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. To be more specific, I'm dealing with a cluster of cases where the lesions have a really strange, textured quality—almost like they have small, jagged protrusions or a very uneven, scaly morphology that doesn't match standard descriptions of psoriasis or eczema. When these types of anomalous, irregular physical features appear, is there a specific way to document these morphological irregularities to avoid the 'unspecified' trap, or should I be looking at specific sub-codes for skin malformations or developmental irregularities?",
